.TH BATTLELINES 1
.SH NAME
battlelines \- swarm combat game
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/battlelines
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I BattleLines
is a swarm combat game.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Two swarms of animated soldiers fight across a green field.
A force circle follows the pointer; hold a button to push your
(light cyan) troops around with it.
With a positive force value, the left button repels troops from
the pointer (red circle) and the right button attracts them
(blue circle); a negative force value inverts both.
Live troop counts for each side are printed at the top right.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B LMB hold
Apply the force field at the pointer
.TP
.B RMB hold
Apply the force field with the opposite sense
.TP
.B mouse wheel buttons 4/8 (if wm sends)
Decrease/increase the signed force value (circle radius)
.TP
.B , / -
Decrease the force value
.TP
.B . / + / =
Increase the force value
.TP
.B 1
Toggle time-lapse: troops are drawn 500 ticks ahead of their true
positions (a display projection; the battle itself runs at normal speed)
.TP
.B 2
Toggle tap-mode: a yellow 50-pixel circle that violently scatters
troops inside it and damps those outside
.TP
.B Enter / r
Restart
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/battlelines.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
